n-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diaphragmatic rupture due to blunt trauma: sensitivity of plain chest radiographs</article-title><source>Am J Roentgenol</source><year>1991</year><volume>156</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1898570</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib-009"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bergin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ennis</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Keogh</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fenlon</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The &#x0201c;dependent viscera&#x0201d; sign in CT diagnosis of blunt traumatic diaphragmatic rupture</article-title><source>Am J Roentgenol</source><year>2001</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>1137</fpage><lpage>1140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11641188</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib-010"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Haciibrahimoglu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Solak</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Olcmen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bedirhan</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Solmazer</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Gurses</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Management of traumatic diaphragmatic rupture</article-title><source>Surg Today</source><year>2004</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14745609</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00595-003-2662-8</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list><glossary><title>Abbreviations</title><def-list id="dl1"><def-item><term>CT</term><def><p>computerized tomography</p></def></def-item><def-item><term>TDH</term><def><p>traumatic diaphragmatic hernia</p></def></def-item></def-list></glossary></back></article>